Audit this circuit for vulnerabilities:

pragma circom 2.0.0;

template UnderdeterminedTemplate() {
   signal input a;
   signal input b;

   a + b === 0;
}

Vulnerability: Underdetermined system (too few constraints).

The circuit has one linear constraint a + b === 0 for two input signals. One equation with two unknowns is underdetermined: many (a, b) pairs satisfy it.

Impact: A prover is not forced to use specific values. For any chosen a, setting b = -a satisfies the constraint. The circuit does not pin down a unique witness unless you add more constraints or bind a and b to a fixed computation.

Fix: Add constraints that fix or uniquely determine the witness (example below pins both inputs to constants; in real circuits you might hash, range-check, or tie inputs to public outputs).

Corrected code:
pragma circom 2.0.0;

template UnderdeterminedTemplate() {
   signal input a;
   signal input b;

   a === 10;
   b === -10;
}

