Vulnerability: Missing boolean constraints on Merkle path indices allow forged proofs

Explanation: `BinaryMerkleRoot` recomputes a Merkle root by selecting, at each level, the ordering of `(node, sibling)` based on the path bit `indices[i]`, using `MultiMux1`. `MultiMux1` only computes `out = c[0] + sel*(c[1]-c[0])`; it never constrains `sel` to be boolean (0 or 1). Here `indices[i]` is a raw input and is never `=== indices[i]*(indices[i]-1) === 0`. A malicious prover can pick a non-boolean `indices[i]` (any field element), which makes `MultiMux1` output an arbitrary affine combination of `nodes[i]` and `siblings[i]` rather than one of the two. By solving for the right `indices[i]` value at each level, the prover can drive the Poseidon chain to produce any target root for an arbitrary leaf, i.e. forge a Merkle membership proof for a leaf that is not in the tree. Since this template gates inclusion of CSCA/DSC certificates and other Merkle-based checks, the entire root-binding guarantee collapses.

Fix: Constrain every element of the `indices` array to be boolean before using it as the mux selector, e.g. `indices[i] * (indices[i] - 1) === 0`, so each path bit can only select one of the two real children.

```circom
pragma circom 2.1.9;

include "circomlib/circuits/mux1.circom";
include "circomlib/circuits/poseidon.circom";
include "circomlib/circuits/comparators.circom";

template BinaryMerkleRoot(MAX_DEPTH) {
    signal input leaf, depth, indices[MAX_DEPTH], siblings[MAX_DEPTH];

    signal output out;

    signal nodes[MAX_DEPTH + 1];
    nodes[0] <== leaf;

    signal roots[MAX_DEPTH];
    var root = 0;

    for (var i = 0; i < MAX_DEPTH; i++) {
        // FIX: force each path index to be a boolean so the mux selects a
        // genuine child and cannot be an arbitrary affine combination.
        indices[i] * (indices[i] - 1) === 0;

        var isDepth = IsEqual()([depth, i]);

        roots[i] <== isDepth * nodes[i];

        root += roots[i];

        var c[2][2] = [ [nodes[i], siblings[i]], [siblings[i], nodes[i]] ];
        var childNodes[2] = MultiMux1(2)(c, indices[i]);

        nodes[i + 1] <== Poseidon(2)(childNodes);
    }

    var isDepth = IsEqual()([depth, MAX_DEPTH]);

    out <== root + isDepth * nodes[MAX_DEPTH];
}
```

