Vulnerability: ArrayXOR output is assigned but not constrained

Explanation: Inside ArrayXOR each output is produced with out[i] <-- a[i] ^ b[i]. The <-- operator is only a witness-generation hint; it emits no R1CS constraint. As a result out[i] is completely under-constrained: a malicious prover is free to assign any value to each out[i] regardless of a[i] and b[i]. Downstream logic (the hash-to-field expansion that relies on this XOR) can thus be driven to arbitrary results, breaking soundness.

