Vulnerability: Membership proof forgeable from any member signature (unconstrained ECDSA inputs)

Explanation: `PubKeyMembership` recovers a public key via `EfficientECDSA()` as `pubKey = s * T + U` and then checks that `Poseidon(pubKeyX, pubKeyY)` is a leaf in the Merkle tree. The catch is that `Tx`, `Ty`, `Ux`, `Uy` are unconstrained private inputs that the prover supplies freely - nothing ties them to a fixed message hash or to the claimed signer. Because the relationship between the signature, the message, and the recovered point is never pinned down, an attacker who learns ANY single valid member signature `s` can choose `T` and `U` so that `s * T + U` equals any target public key already in the tree. The circuit then produces a valid membership proof for a victim the attacker does not control, defeating the soundness of the membership check.

Fix: Bind the ECDSA verification inputs to a specific message and recovered public key so the prover cannot freely pick `Tx`, `Ty`, `Ux`, `Uy`. Pass in the message hash `msgHash` and derive `T` and `U` from it inside the circuit (the canonical eff-ECDSA derivation), so the membership proof is only valid for a signature over a known message by the actual member.

```circom
pragma circom 2.1.2;

include "eff_ecdsa.circom";
include "tree.circom";
include "poseidon.circom";

template PubKeyMembership(nLevels) {
    signal input s;
    signal input msgHash;       // bind verification to a concrete message
    signal input Tx;
    signal input Ty;
    signal input Ux;
    signal input Uy;

    signal input root;
    signal input pathIndices[nLevels];
    signal input siblings[nLevels];

    // Constrain (Tx,Ty) and (Ux,Uy) to the canonical points derived from msgHash
    // and the curve generator, so they are no longer free inputs.
    component derive = EffEcdsaDerivePoints();
    derive.msgHash <== msgHash;
    derive.Tx === Tx;
    derive.Ty === Ty;
    derive.Ux === Ux;
    derive.Uy === Uy;

    component ecdsa = EfficientECDSA();
    ecdsa.s <== s;
    ecdsa.Tx <== Tx;
    ecdsa.Ty <== Ty;
    ecdsa.Ux <== Ux;
    ecdsa.Uy <== Uy;

    component pubKeyHash = Poseidon(2);
    pubKeyHash.inputs[0] <== ecdsa.pubKeyX;
    pubKeyHash.inputs[1] <== ecdsa.pubKeyY;

    component merkleProof = MerkleTreeInclusionProof(nLevels);
    merkleProof.leaf <== pubKeyHash.out;
    for (var i = 0; i < nLevels; i++) {
        merkleProof.pathIndices[i] <== pathIndices[i];
        merkleProof.siblings[i] <== siblings[i];
    }
    merkleProof.root === root;
}
