pragma circom 2.1.2;

include "../../node_modules/circomlib/circuits/comparators.circom";

template hydraS2(registryTreeHeight, accountsTreeHeight) {
    // ... merkle membership, commitment mapper, nullifier logic elided ...

    signal input sourceValue;          // PRIVATE: claimed account value
    signal input statementValue;       // PUBLIC: value being asserted
    signal input statementComparator;  // PUBLIC: 0 = GTE, 1 = EQ

    // BUG: the lower-bound comparison is always enforced, regardless of the
    // statementComparator flag. Producing any valid proof reveals to the
    // verifier that statementValue <= sourceValue, leaking info about the
    // private sourceValue.
    component leq = LessEqThan(252);
    leq.in[0] <== statementValue;
    leq.in[1] <== sourceValue;
    leq.out === 1;

    // statementComparator only optionally adds the equality constraint.
    sourceValue === sourceValue + ((statementValue - sourceValue) * statementComparator);
}
```

Vulnerability: Unconditional lower-bound check leaks private sourceValue in hydraS2

Explanation: The circuit unconditionally enforces `LessEqThan(252)` with `leq.out === 1`, i.e. `statementValue <= sourceValue`, before applying the `statementComparator`-gated equality. The `statementComparator` flag only decides whether equality is ALSO required (when it is 1, `sourceValue === statementValue`); it never disables the lower-bound check. As a result, any time a valid proof is produced - even with `statementComparator = 0`, which a user picks precisely to keep their value hidden - the verifier learns the inequality `statementValue <= sourceValue`, a public lower bound on the private `sourceValue`. This is a privacy / information-leakage flaw: the private input is partially disclosed whenever the comparison is on, with no way for the prover to turn it off.

Fix: Make enabling the lower-bound comparison explicit, just as the equality check is gated. Introduce a `statementComparisonEnabled` public flag and replace `leq.out === 1;` with `(leq.out - 1) * statementComparisonEnabled === 0;`, so the comparison (and its leakage) is fully turned off when the user does not opt in to revealing a lower bound on `sourceValue`.

```circom
pragma circom 2.1.2;

include "../../node_modules/circomlib/circuits/comparators.circom";

template hydraS2(registryTreeHeight, accountsTreeHeight) {
    // ... merkle membership, commitment mapper, nullifier logic elided ...

    signal input sourceValue;               // PRIVATE
    signal input statementValue;            // PUBLIC
    signal input statementComparator;       // PUBLIC: 0 = GTE, 1 = EQ
    signal input statementComparisonEnabled; // PUBLIC: 1 = enforce lower bound

    // Gate the lower-bound comparison so it can be disabled to avoid leakage.
    component leq = LessEqThan(252);
    leq.in[0] <== statementValue;
    leq.in[1] <== sourceValue;
    (leq.out - 1) * statementComparisonEnabled === 0;

    // Equality is still optionally enforced via statementComparator.
    sourceValue === sourceValue + ((statementValue - sourceValue) * statementComparator);
}
```

