Vulnerability: Missing do_not_emit! constraints in the DecodeTagStart => LongList transition

Explanation: A `LongList` header byte (`0xf8 <= byte_value`) is only the start of a list — the current row does not represent a fully decoded tag value, so it must not produce an output row in the `RlpFsmRlpTable`. Every other partial-decode transition in this FSM (e.g. `DecodeTagStart => Bytes`, `DecodeTagStart => LongBytes`, the `LongList => LongList` step) invokes the `do_not_emit!` macro, which forces `rlp_table.is_output = false`. This `DecodeTagStart => LongList` gate omits `do_not_emit!` entirely, so `is_output` on these header rows is left unconstrained. A malicious prover can set `is_output = true` (with arbitrary `rlp_tag` / `tag_value`) on a LongList header row, injecting an invalid row into the `RlpFsmRlpTable` that other circuits trust via lookups. This is a critical soundness bug from a wrong translation of the FSM logic into constraints.

Fix: Add the missing `do_not_emit!` constraint in the `DecodeTagStart => LongList` transition so `is_output` is forced to false for these non-terminal header rows.

```rust
// state transition: DecodeTagStart => LongList
meta.create_gate("state transition: DecodeTagStart => LongList", |meta| {
    let mut cb = BaseConstraintBuilder::default();

    let (bv_gt_0xf8, bv_eq_0xf8) = byte_value_gte_0xf8.expr(meta, None);

    let cond = and::expr([
        sum::expr([bv_gt_0xf8, bv_eq_0xf8]),
        not::expr(is_tag_end_expr(meta)),
    ]);
    cb.condition(cond.expr(), |cb| {
        // assertions.
        do_not_emit!(meta, cb);
        constrain_eq!(meta, cb, is_tag_begin, true);

        // state transitions
        update_state!(meta, cb, tag_length, byte_value_expr(meta) - 0xf7.expr());
        update_state!(meta, cb, tag_idx, 1);
        update_state!(meta, cb, tag_value_acc, byte_value_next_expr(meta));
        update_state!(meta, cb, state, State::LongList);

        constrain_unchanged_fields!(meta, cb; rlp_table.tx_id, rlp_table.format, tag, tag_next);
    });

    cb.gate(and::expr([
        meta.query_fixed(q_enabled, Rotation::cur()),
        is_decode_tag_start(meta),
    ]))
});
