Vulnerability: RLP FSM does not constrain tag_value to equal the accumulated tag_value_acc

Explanation: In the RLP circuit's state machine, the `Bytes` state folds each decoded byte into `tag_value_acc` via `tag_value_acc' = tag_value_acc * b + next_byte`. When `tag_idx == tag_length` (`tidx_eq_tlen`), the machine transitions `Bytes => DecodeTagStart` and emits the RLP tag using `emit_rlp_tag!`, which constrains `is_output`, `rlp_tag`, and `is_none` on `rlp_table` -- but it never constrains `rlp_table.tag_value` against the accumulated `tag_value_acc`. Because the emitted `rlp_table.tag_value` is otherwise free, a malicious prover can write an arbitrary value into the RLP table's `tag_value` column that differs from the value actually decoded from the byte stream. Downstream circuits (e.g. the Tx circuit) trust this RLP table, so an attacker can inject a forged field value (nonce, gas, value, etc.) that was never present in the real RLP encoding.

Fix: On the `Bytes => DecodeTagStart` transition (when `tag_idx == tag_length`), add a constraint requiring `rlp_table.tag_value == tag_value_acc`, so the emitted tag value must equal the value accumulated over all of the tag's bytes.

```rust
meta.create_gate("state transition: Bytes", |meta| {
    let mut cb = BaseConstraintBuilder::default();

    let (tidx_lt_tlen, tidx_eq_tlen) = tidx_lte_tlength.expr(meta, None);
    let (mlen_lt_0x20, mlen_eq_0x20) = mlength_lte_0x20.expr(meta, None);

    let b = select::expr(
        mlen_lt_0x20,
        256.expr(),
        select::expr(mlen_eq_0x20, evm_word_rand, keccak_input_rand),
    );

    // Bytes => Bytes
    cb.condition(tidx_lt_tlen, |cb| {
        do_not_emit!(meta, cb);
        update_state!(meta, cb, tag_idx, tag_idx_expr(meta) + 1.expr());
        update_state!(meta, cb, tag_value_acc,
            tag_value_acc_expr(meta) * b.expr() + byte_value_next_expr(meta));
        update_state!(meta, cb, state, State::Bytes);
        constrain_unchanged_fields!(meta, cb; depth, tag, tag_next, tag_length, rlp_table.tx_id, rlp_table.format);
    });

    // Bytes => DecodeTagStart
    cb.condition(tidx_eq_tlen, |cb| {
        // assertions
        emit_rlp_tag!(meta, cb, tag_expr(meta), false);
        // The emitted tag_value must equal the fully accumulated tag_value_acc
        // (tag_idx has reached tag_length, so all bytes have been folded in).
        constrain_eq!(meta, cb, rlp_table.tag_value, tag_value_acc_expr(meta));

        // state transitions.
        update_state!(meta, cb, tag, tag_next_expr(meta));
        update_state!(meta, cb, state, State::DecodeTagStart);

        constrain_unchanged_fields!(meta, cb; rlp_table.tx_id, rlp_table.format, depth);
    });

    cb.gate(and::expr([
        meta.query_fixed(q_enabled, Rotation::cur()),
        is_bytes(meta),
    ]))
});
```

