Vulnerability: Soundness failure due to 0 value not enforced

Explanation: `selector_dot_product` computes the dot product of the one-hot `selector` with `value_vector` by using `pick` to choose, for each entry, either the value (when the selection bit is 1) or `zero` (when the bit is 0). Here `zero` is allocated via `AllocatedNum::alloc` but never constrained to actually be 0. Because it is assigned-but-unconstrained, a malicious prover can witness any value for `zero`; that value is then added into the sum for every unselected entry, so the final `result` can be shifted to an arbitrary number. Since this gadget backs `case`/`multi_case` selection, the attacker controls selected outputs and breaks soundness.

Fix: Do not allocate a fresh `zero` inside the gadget. Pass in the previously allocated and constrained zero variable from the global store (`g.false_num`), which is guaranteed to remain 0, so the default product for unselected entries cannot be manipulated.

```rust
