Vulnerability: Vectors not constrained to be of the same size

Explanation: `multi_case_aux` constrains the selector once from `cases[0]` and then reuses it across every other clause group, zipping the selector with each group's values and pairing each group with its default. The code never checks that `cases.len() == defaults.len()`, that the groups are non-empty, or that every clause group has the same length. When the vectors disagree in size the `zip` truncates silently: clause values without a selector bit (or vice versa) are dropped, so the corresponding outputs are left unconstrained, and in other configurations the mismatch causes a runtime crash. This wrong translation of logic into constraints can hide soundness bugs.

Fix: Add assertions at the top of the gadget to guarantee the inputs are consistently sized before any constraints are generated: `cases` and `defaults` must have equal length, `cases` and each group must be non-empty, and all clause groups must have the same length.

