Vulnerability: Unsound fixed-point multiplication

Explanation: `U128x128Var::checked_mul` multiplies two 128.128 fixed-point values by forming the schoolbook limb products `z0..z6` and then must (a) scale the 256-bit-fractional product back by `2^-128` (truncating the low 128 bits) and (b) recombine the running temporaries `t_i` into four 64-bit result limbs while carrying overflow upward. The bug is that this overflow/truncation accounting is not constrained: the carry pulled out of each `t_i` is just re-packed from prover-supplied bits via `le_bits_to_fp_var(...to_bits_le())`, with no constraint proving `t_i` fits in its expected width or that `t_i = w_i + carry*2^64`. A malicious prover can choose inconsistent carries, so the circuit accepts a `w0..w3` that is not the correct scaled product, an unsound multiplication that is especially dangerous for the financial calculations it backs.

Fix: Correctly constrain each limb of the result. For every temporary, use a `bit_constrain` helper to prove it fits in the expected bit-width, then take the low 64 bits as the result limb and the high bits as the carry into the next temporary, so the truncation by `2^-128` and the carry propagation are enforced by range constraints, and constrain the top product `z6 == 0` for no overflow.

```rust
pub fn checked_mul(self, rhs: &Self) -> Result<U128x128Var, SynthesisError> {
    let x0 = Boolean::<Fq>::le_bits_to_fp_var(&self.limbs[0].to_bits_le())?;
    let x1 = Boolean::<Fq>::le_bits_to_fp_var(&self.limbs[1].to_bits_le())?;
    let x2 = Boolean::<Fq>::le_bits_to_fp_var(&self.limbs[2].to_bits_le())?;
    let x3 = Boolean::<Fq>::le_bits_to_fp_var(&self.limbs[3].to_bits_le())?;
    let y0 = Boolean::<Fq>::le_bits_to_fp_var(&rhs.limbs[0].to_bits_le())?;
    let y1 = Boolean::<Fq>::le_bits_to_fp_var(&rhs.limbs[1].to_bits_le())?;
    let y2 = Boolean::<Fq>::le_bits_to_fp_var(&rhs.limbs[2].to_bits_le())?;
    let y3 = Boolean::<Fq>::le_bits_to_fp_var(&rhs.limbs[3].to_bits_le())?;

    let z0 = &x0 * &y0;
    let z1 = &x0 * &y1 + &x1 * &y0;
    let z2 = &x0 * &y2 + &x1 * &y1 + &x2 * &y0;
    let z3 = &x0 * &y3 + &x1 * &y2 + &x2 * &y1 + &x3 * &y0;
    let z4 = &x1 * &y3 + &x2 * &y2 + &x3 * &y1;
    let z5 = &x2 * &y3 + &x3 * &y2;
    let z6 = &x3 * &y3;

    // Each temporary is range-constrained, enforcing the (low limb, carry) split.
    let t0 = z0 + z1 * Fq::from(1u128 << 64);
    let t0_bits = bit_constrain(t0, 193)?;
    let t1 = z2 + Boolean::<Fq>::le_bits_to_fp_var(&t0_bits[128..193].to_bits_le()?)?;
    let t1_bits = bit_constrain(t1, 129)?;
    let w0 = UInt64::from_bits_le(&t0_bits[0..64]);

    let t2 = z3 + Boolean::<Fq>::le_bits_to_fp_var(&t1_bits[64..129].to_bits_le()?)?;
    let t2_bits = bit_constrain(t2, 129)?;
    let w1 = UInt64::from_bits_le(&t2_bits[0..64]);

    let t3 = z4 + Boolean::<Fq>::le_bits_to_fp_var(&t2_bits[64..129].to_bits_le()?)?;
    let t3_bits = bit_constrain(t3, 129)?;
    let w2 = UInt64::from_bits_le(&t3_bits[0..64]);

    let t4 = z5 + Boolean::<Fq>::le_bits_to_fp_var(&t3_bits[64..129].to_bits_le()?)?;
    let t4_bits = bit_constrain(t4, 64)?; // if we did not overflow, fits in 64 bits
    let w3 = UInt64::from_bits_le(&t4_bits[0..64]);

    // No overflow.
    z6.enforce_equal(&FqVar::zero())?;
    Ok(U128x128Var { limbs: [w0, w1, w2, w3] })
}
```

