Vulnerability: Rust verifier never validates the proof's vk_root against the expected root

Explanation: This is SP1's native Rust verifier (`crates/prover/src/verify.rs`). The recursion public values carry `vk_root`, the Merkle root over the set of all legitimate recursion verifying-key hashes; the recursive circuit and on-chain verifier check that this root equals the expected precomputed value so only sanctioned verifying keys can be used. `verify_compressed` (and likewise `verify_shrink` and `verify_deferred_proof`) only checks membership of the leaf vk in `recursion_vk_map` and the `sp1_vk_digest`, but never validates `public_values.vk_root` against `self.recursion_vk_root`. A malicious prover can therefore embed an arbitrary/invalid `vk_root` in the public values and still pass the native verifier, decoupling the proof's claimed verifying-key set from the trusted one, a soundness break (the circuit/on-chain verifiers were not affected because they perform this check).

Fix: Add an explicit `vk_root` check in `verify_compressed`, `verify_shrink`, and `verify_deferred_proof`: if `public_values.vk_root != self.recursion_vk_root` return `InvalidPublicValues`. Implemented in SP1 v5.0.0 (commit aa9a8e40).

```rust
/// Verify a compressed proof.
pub fn verify_compressed(
    &self,
    proof: &SP1ReduceProof<BabyBearPoseidon2>,
    vk: &SP1VerifyingKey,
) -> Result<(), MachineVerificationError<CoreSC>> {
    let SP1ReduceProof { vk: compress_vk, proof } = proof;
    let mut challenger = self.compress_prover.config().challenger();
    let machine_proof = MachineProof { shard_proofs: vec![proof.clone()] };
    self.compress_prover.machine().verify(compress_vk, &machine_proof, &mut challenger)?;

    let public_values: &RecursionPublicValues<_> = proof.public_values.as_slice().borrow();
    assert_recursion_public_values_valid(self.compress_prover.machine().config(), public_values);

    if self.vk_verification && !self.recursion_vk_map.contains_key(&compress_vk.hash_babybear()) {
        return Err(MachineVerificationError::InvalidVerificationKey);
    }

    // Validate the proof's vk_root against the expected precomputed recursion vk_root.
    if public_values.vk_root != self.recursion_vk_root {
        return Err(MachineVerificationError::InvalidPublicValues("vk_root mismatch"));
    }

    if public_values.is_complete != BabyBear::one() {
        return Err(MachineVerificationError::InvalidPublicValues("is_complete is not 1"));
    }

    let vkey_hash = vk.hash_babybear();
    if public_values.sp1_vk_digest != vkey_hash {
        return Err(MachineVerificationError::InvalidPublicValues("sp1 vk hash mismatch"));
    }
    Ok(())
}
